// backends/mini/src/runtime/miniBridge.sla — full retranslation of
// miniBridge.ts (CXU plugins @ f2cb649d, 10,282 lines).
// Model: _defects/FIX_SAVMTOOL.md (sa_json path-addressed handles, status
// codes for try/catch), _defects/FIX_RELAY_GATEWAY.md (giant-file batch
// method), ledger: _defects/FIX_MINIBRIDGE.md.
//
// Representation (registered in the ledger):
// - Dynamic records (MiniSession, MiniSnapshot, JSON-RPC params/results,
//   wire messages, tool calls) are JSON text carried in MbJson/MbBig and
//   manipulated through sa_json doc handles (path addressing). A session
//   IS its snapshot-shaped JSON object; class fields that are Maps in TS
//   are JSON objects keyed by id inside the MiniBridge state record.
// - EventEmitter is NOT modeled (CAPABILITY_MAP four-source verdict:
//   confirmed unsupported). Events are an ordered JSON queue on the
//   bridge plus a listener registry; see MiniBridge_on / MiniBridge_emit /
//   MiniBridge_drain_events in the class section. No EventEmitter stub.
// - TS async fns land as synchronous fns (ASYNC_MODEL blocking contract):
//   every awaited surface used here (fs, http client, process, MCP/host
//   seams) is a blocking extern or an in-process call in sa_std/the tree;
//   control flow is 1:1 and each site is registered in the ledger.
//   Timers/abort land as deadline fields + poll points (timer model).

